(text "BUF_N16: Y1 = A1, Y2 = A2. One 6N16B (6Н16Б): two independent cathode followers (owner, 2026-10-28).\nEach: plate to +150 V; cathode -> Rs 2.2k || Cs 100p -> Y -> Rk 12k -> -50 V. Rs puts Y ~5 V below the cathode,\nso '0' is about -19 V although the cathode sits 5 V above its grid, and it limits the load grid current on a '1'.\nInput: LV (1 = +10 V, 0 = -20 V), from its OWN divider on the driving HV net: 470k || C1 / 200k to -50 V,\nC1 = 2.7 pF per follower grid. Never share that divider with gate grids (NOT/NOR/NAND): they clamp a '1' at\n+0.4 V and Y then stays near -5 V. Output Y: LV, straight onto gate grids (no divider); fanout 10 grids.\nY must not drive another BUF_N16/OR2_N16 input or any HV input. Supplies: +150 V, -50 V, heater 6.3 V 0.4 A.\nSimulated, fanout 2/10 (input grid -5 V -> load plate 100 V): Y up 24/69 ns, Y down 32/224 ns. Ik 5.4 mA, Pa 0.74 W.\nPage: sch/logic/BUF_N16/README.md" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 177.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "99ee81e4-0881-4fa9-9ad9-ce2badd0c0cc"))

